WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:02.400
A new team does not need all the answers

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.590
on day one, it needs a way to hear

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.680
everyone.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.700
Meet Northstar Studio, a fictional tech company building project

00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:10.400
Beacon.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.630
Maya manages the team, Priya leads product, Eli and

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:18.240
Ben are engineers, Jules is the architect.

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.080
Their first customers, their platform and their way of

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:23.040
working are still open questions.

00:00:23.324 --> 00:00:26.337
Maya creates a call and answer engagement.

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:28.876
She gives it a title, chooses the team's custom

00:00:29.439 --> 00:00:32.956
questions, and adds a short project brief for Workie.

00:00:33.015 --> 00:00:35.455
The team has six weeks to learn and test

00:00:35.514 --> 00:00:36.996
one useful idea.

00:00:37.154 --> 00:00:40.769
These details give the discussion a clear starting point.

00:00:40.838 --> 00:00:42.419
Then she opens the room.

00:00:42.578 --> 00:00:45.224
People scan the code or open the join link

00:00:45.264 --> 00:00:46.607
and type their name.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.344
No account is needed.

00:00:48.384 --> 00:00:50.635
Priya joins from her laptop.

00:00:50.674 --> 00:00:52.491
Jules uses a tablet.

00:00:52.530 --> 00:00:55.176
A laptop or tablet works best here.

00:00:55.216 --> 00:00:57.477
There is more typing than in trivia or a

00:00:57.477 --> 00:00:58.612
survey.

00:00:58.652 --> 00:01:01.179
Back on the host screen, all five teammates are

00:01:01.238 --> 00:01:01.811
ready.

00:01:01.981 --> 00:01:04.756
The first question asks who Beacon should learn from

00:01:04.756 --> 00:01:06.283
first and why.

00:01:06.333 --> 00:01:09.317
Each person writes an answer on their own screen.

00:01:09.607 --> 00:01:12.591
Priya wants to speak with small software teams.

00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:16.424
Jules suggests internal platform teams.

00:01:16.474 --> 00:01:18.460
Different roles see different risks.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:21.065
Everyone gets time to put a clear idea into

00:01:21.195 --> 00:01:23.251
words before the room compares them.

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.112
Maya opens voting.

00:01:25.171 --> 00:01:28.286
The room reads the answers without names attached, so

00:01:28.286 --> 00:01:30.788
the ideas can stand on their own.

00:01:30.867 --> 00:01:34.922
Each teammate ranks their first, second, and third choices.

00:01:34.981 --> 00:01:37.454
Priya makes her picks and submits them.

00:01:37.513 --> 00:01:40.292
The host can see when all five votes are

00:01:40.292 --> 00:01:42.280
in, then reveal the result.

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:45.517
The results show which ideas drew support.

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.974
Workie reads the responses in light of the project

00:01:48.654 --> 00:01:51.291
brief and pulls out points for the team to

00:01:51.291 --> 00:01:52.150
discuss.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.827
This is a starting point for judgment, not a

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:56.586
decision made for them.

00:01:56.636 --> 00:01:59.712
Maya opens a feedback round so people can add

00:01:59.712 --> 00:02:02.120
what is missing or challenge an assumption.

00:02:02.319 --> 00:02:04.773
Priya adds a concrete follow-up.

00:02:04.852 --> 00:02:07.849
Ask customers to show the last request that got

00:02:07.849 --> 00:02:08.532
lost.

00:02:08.611 --> 00:02:10.412
Jules flags a risk.

00:02:10.412 --> 00:02:12.974
A useful internal tool may not be a product

00:02:12.974 --> 00:02:14.488
someone will buy.

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:17.021
Their feedback stays with the round.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.791
The team then moves on to a small experiment

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.314
and a working agreement.

00:02:21.393 --> 00:02:23.283
They are shaping a plan together.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.963
After the discussion, Maya opens the session report.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.514
The questions, responses, votes, and feedback give the team

00:02:30.514 --> 00:02:32.017
a record to return to.

00:02:32.094 --> 00:02:34.984
She saves the report and downloads a copy.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:37.836
Start with your own questions and the situation your

00:02:37.846 --> 00:02:39.023
team faces.

00:02:39.023 --> 00:02:41.933
A new platform, a hard choice, or a better

00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:42.967
way to work.

00:02:43.043 --> 00:02:44.766
What will you build?
